# CH. 1: Today's Security Professional

---

## 1. Core Security Concepts

### Security Objectives vs. Threats (CIA vs. DAD)

| CIA Triad (Objective) | Description | DAD Triad (Threat) | Description / Examples |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Confidentiality** | Ensures unauthorized users (`unAUs`) are not able to gain access. | **Disclosure** | Exposure of sensitive info to unauthorized users (data loss, data exfiltration). |
| **Integrity** | Ensures no unauthorized users modify info or the system. | **Alteration** | Unauthorized modification of info (e.g., fraudulent transactions, typos). |
| **Availability** | Ensures info/system is ready to meet the needs of a legitimate user. | **Denial** | Disruption of authorized users' legitimate access (e.g., DDoS). |

> **Non-repudiation:** Ensures someone who performed an action cannot deny having taken it (e.g., Digital Signatures).

